.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NQERR 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqerr ,
.Nm nqver
.Nd error messages and the library version
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft const char *
.Fn nqerr "int err"
.Ft const char *
.Fn nqver void
.Fd #define NQVMAJ
.Fd #define NQVMIN
.Fd #define NQVPAT
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Every function of
.Xr noqtis 3
that can fail returns
.Dv NQOK
(0) or one of these negative codes:
.Bl -column "NQESTATE" "-10" -offset indent
.It Sy code Ta Sy value Ta Sy nqerr text
.It Dv NQOK Ta 0 Ta success
.It Dv NQEARG Ta \-1 Ta invalid argument
.It Dv NQEBUF Ta \-2 Ta output buffer too small
.It Dv NQEVRFY Ta \-3 Ta verification failed
.It Dv NQEDEC Ta \-4 Ta input is not in the encoding the standard defines
.It Dv NQERNG Ta \-5 Ta the operating system's random source failed
.It Dv NQEMEM Ta \-6 Ta out of memory
.It Dv NQEIO Ta \-7 Ta file could not be read or written
.It Dv NQENOSUP Ta \-8 Ta algorithm or option not supported
.It Dv NQELIM Ta \-9 Ta input exceeds a size or depth limit
.It Dv NQESTATE Ta \-10 Ta context used out of order
.El
.Pp
.Fn nqerr
returns the English text of
.Fa err
from the table, or
.Dq unknown error
for any other value.
The strings are static; do not free them.
.Pp
A failed verification is always
.Er NQEVRFY
(or another negative code), never
.Dv NQOK .
Test for success with
.Ql rc == NQOK ,
never with
.Ql rc >= 0
or by truth value alone.
.Pp
.Fn nqver
returns the version of the library as linked,
.Dq Ar major . Ns Ar minor . Ns Ar patch .
.Dv NQVMAJ ,
.Dv NQVMIN
and
.Dv NQVPAT
give the version of the header a program was compiled with.
The library follows semantic versioning; its shared-library ABI version is
the major version.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Both functions return a pointer to a static string, never
.Dv NULL .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
int rc = nqvrfy(alg, pk, pklen, msg, msglen, NULL, 0, 0, sig, siglen);
if (rc != NQOK)
  fprintf(stderr, "verify: %s\en", nqerr(rc));
printf("built with %d.%d.%d, running %s\en", NQVMAJ, NQVMIN, NQVPAT,
       nqver());
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 3
